<abstract xml:lang="zh"><p>城市公园土壤承担着调节径流、储存碳和支持植物生长等重要生态系统功能，但与自然土壤相比，其微生物群落研究要少得多。本简报介绍了对某匿名大城市中六座公园土壤细菌群落进行宏条形码分析的初步结果，这些公园在建园年代和游憩利用强度方面各不相同。从草坪、林冠下区域和步道沿线共采集了 72 份表层土壤样品。通过对 16S rRNA 基因 V4 可变区进行测序确定群落组成；同时测定了 pH、有机碳含量、土壤容重和重金属浓度。细菌 α 多样性在老公园的林冠下最高，在压实的步道沿线最低。群落结构在不同样地类型之间存在显著差异（PERMANOVA，R² = 0.21），在不同公园之间的差异则较小。决定群落组成的最重要因素是 pH 和土壤容重，而在所研究的浓度范围内，重金属的影响较弱。这些数据表明，公园的管理方式和空间布局对土壤微生物多样性的影响至少不亚于污染。目前研究仍在继续，将扩大样本并纳入真菌群落。</p></abstract>
<trans-abstract xml:lang="en"><p>The soils of urban parks perform important ecosystem functions, regulating runoff, storing carbon and supporting plant growth, yet their microbial communities have been studied far less than those of natural soils. This short communication presents the first results of metabarcoding of bacterial communities in the soils of six parks in an anonymised large city that differ in age and intensity of recreational use. Seventy-two samples of the topsoil were collected from lawns, areas under tree cover and along footpaths. Community composition was determined by sequencing the V4 variable region of the 16S rRNA gene; pH, organic carbon content, soil bulk density and heavy metal concentrations were measured in parallel. Bacterial alpha diversity was highest under tree cover in older parks and lowest along compacted paths. Community structure differed significantly between site types (PERMANOVA, R² = 0.21) and to a lesser extent between parks. The most important factors shaping community composition were pH and bulk density, whereas the effect of heavy metals at the concentrations studied was weak. These data suggest that park management and layout influence soil microbial diversity at least as much as pollution does. Work is continuing with an expanded sample and the inclusion of fungal communities.</p></trans-abstract>
